# Feed API (client parity)

This application **consumes** the feed API implemented by **[dp1-feed-v2](https://github.com/display-protocol/dp1-feed-v2)**. The normative specification is **[api/openapi.yaml](https://github.com/display-protocol/dp1-feed-v2/blob/main/api/openapi.yaml)**, with **[docs/api_design.md](https://github.com/display-protocol/dp1-feed-v2/blob/main/docs/api_design.md)** as narrative.

When changing HTTP usage, payloads, pagination, caching headers, or error handling:

- reconcile with **OpenAPI + api_design**, and note any intentional subset or deviation in code/comments or `docs/architecture.md`
- preserve stable **`error` codes** in branching logic (`FeedAPIError`); treat **`message`** as human-readable and variable

## Versioning & metadata

- Base path **`/api/v1`**; **`GET /api/v1`** yields deployment metadata (**`extensionsEnabled`**, endpoints, etc.) unless **`VITE_DP1_EXTENSIONS_ENABLED`** overrides UX locally (`DEVELOPMENT.md`).

## Auth model (publisher path)

- Browser flows rely on **`signatures`** on DP-1 JSON for operator writes where the feed allows **signature-only** auth; feeds may combine with API-key rules for tooling not in this UI.
- Do not embed feed API keys in client code.

## Resources (shape)

Plural segments mirror the server (`playlists`, `playlist-groups`, `channels`, `playlist-items`; registry routes as implemented). Kebab-case path segments stay stable with server routes.

## JSON & listings

Prefer types that match server field names (`items`, `hasMore`, `cursor`). Handle pagination semantics consistently in list views.

## Errors

Expect JSON like `{"error":"<stable_code>","message":"<detail>"}` when the feed returns structured errors — map alongside raw HTTP failures.

## Compatibility

Additive server changes should be tolerated in the client where reasonable; breaking changes require coordinated deployment or versioning strategy—call out rollout risk in PRs/plans.

